 "text": "Gold is a symbolic metal the Celts linked to the sun and to the growth of summer plants. Its worth lay in trade and in myth alike, and the Celts were famed as metalworkers. This made gold a favored metal for rings and neck-rings. Twisted gold collars called torcs count among treasures of the ancient craft, and ritual finds such as the gold boat at Broighter Bog confirm its value.",
